@baseUrl = https://s-traccceer.vinfocom.co.in
@clientId = drive-app
@uploaderKey = REPLACE_SECURELY
@reportingKey = REPLACE_SECURELY
@uploadId = 7d8d4442-21b3-4a60-a3dc-b7b96c9f062c
@leaseToken = REPLACE_FROM_CLAIM_RESPONSE
@region = IN
@authCookie = REPLACE_WITH_EXISTING_LOGIN_AUTH_COOKIE
@csrfToken = REPLACE_WITH_CSRF_COOKIE_VALUE
@recipientId = REPLACE_FROM_RECIPIENT_REGISTRATION
@deliveryId = REPLACE_FROM_EMAIL_DELIVERIES

### OPTIONAL company admin: register ADDITIONAL recipients BEFORE registering the ZIP upload.
# The valid tbl_company.email is included automatically at ZIP registration; no POST is needed for it.
# Use an existing company admin login cookie (role 2 or 3). Scope comes from that login.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/recipients
Cookie: st.auth={{authCookie}}; st.csrf={{csrfToken}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"rf-team@example.com","name":"RF reporting team"}

### Company admin: list report subscriptions, including companyDefault=true company-managed email.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/recipients
Cookie: st.auth={{authCookie}}; st.csrf={{csrfToken}}

### Company admin: inspect email delivery status independently of report generation.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/email-deliveries?uploadId={{uploadId}}
Cookie: st.auth={{authCookie}}; st.csrf={{csrfToken}}

### Company admin: retry a dead-letter email without regenerating the PDF.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/email-deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/retry
Cookie: st.auth={{authCookie}}; st.csrf={{csrfToken}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

### Company admin: unsubscribe an additional recipient and cancel queued emails.
# An enabled companyDefault=true address returns 409; its address comes from the company profile.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/recipients/{{recipientId}}
Cookie: st.auth={{authCookie}}; st.csrf={{csrfToken}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

### One-call app route: POST /api/rf-logs/upload, multipart file/uploadId/sessionId.
# See rf-client-integration.http for its complete request and rf-app-single-api.md for the contract.
# Backend uploads to S3 and records completion; do not also run the flow below for that ZIP.

### Optional direct-to-S3 flow 1. Existing logged-in app requests a private upload URL. Use REAL session/project IDs.
# Login remains POST /api/auth/login; reuse its cookies. User/company come from the login.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/uploads
Cookie: st.auth={{authCookie}}; st.csrf={{csrfToken}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "uploadId": "{{uploadId}}",
  "fileName": "drive-test.zip",
  "fileSizeBytes": 524293392,
  "sessionId": 4266,
  "subSessionId": "20",
  "projectId": 123
}

### 2. PUT ZIP bytes to uploadUrl from response (outside this backend).
# PUT <uploadUrl>
# Content-Type: application/zip
# Body: raw binary ZIP, not multipart/form-data. Do not attach API-key headers.

### 3. Call only after the PUT succeeds. Retries use the SAME uploadId.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/uploads/{{uploadId}}/complete
Cookie: st.auth={{authCookie}}; st.csrf={{csrfToken}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

### 4. Uploader can query the accepted event/report status.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/uploads/{{uploadId}}
Cookie: st.auth={{authCookie}}; st.csrf={{csrfToken}}

### Optional: trusted server-to-server uploader (not mobile/browser). Company-scoped key.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/uploads
X-RF-Client-Id: {{clientId}}
X-RF-Api-Key: {{uploaderKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"uploadId":"{{uploadId}}","fileName":"drive.zip","fileSizeBytes":100,"sessionId":4266,"userId":456}

### Reporting service: poll when an incoming webhook receiver is not configured.
# For an external report engine, set AutomaticReportsEnabled=false; otherwise the built-in PDF worker consumes jobs.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/events?limit=25
X-RF-Api-Key: {{reportingKey}}
X-RF-Region: {{region}}

### Reporting service: claim BEFORE generating a report.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/events/{{uploadId}}/claim
X-RF-Api-Key: {{reportingKey}}
X-RF-Region: {{region}}

### Reporting service: get a fresh, short-lived download URL.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/events/{{uploadId}}/download
X-RF-Api-Key: {{reportingKey}}
X-RF-Region: {{region}}

### Renew lease every <15 minutes during long jobs (same endpoint accepts completed/failed).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/events/{{uploadId}}/status
X-RF-Api-Key: {{reportingKey}}
X-RF-Region: {{region}}
X-RF-Lease-Token: {{leaseToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"status":"processing"}

### Record success. reportReference is an identifier/path, not a server-fetched URL.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/events/{{uploadId}}/status
X-RF-Api-Key: {{reportingKey}}
X-RF-Region: {{region}}
X-RF-Lease-Token: {{leaseToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"status":"completed","reportReference":"reports/7d8d4442-21b3-4a60-a3dc-b7b96c9f062c.pdf"}

### Delivery diagnostics.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/events/{{uploadId}}
X-RF-Api-Key: {{reportingKey}}
X-RF-Region: {{region}}

### Re-deliver an upload notification (also works after automatic report completion).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/events/{{uploadId}}/notification-retry
X-RF-Api-Key: {{reportingKey}}
X-RF-Region: {{region}}

### Logged-in uploader: download a completed automatic PDF.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/uploads/{{uploadId}}/report
Cookie: st.auth={{authCookie}}; st.csrf={{csrfToken}}

### Logged-in uploader: requeue a failed report.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/uploads/{{uploadId}}/report-retry
Cookie: st.auth={{authCookie}}; st.csrf={{csrfToken}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

### Reporting service: download the completed automatic PDF.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rf-logs/events/{{uploadId}}/report
X-RF-Api-Key: {{reportingKey}}
X-RF-Region: {{region}}
